a = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
a.remove(3)  #//The remove() method is used to remove the first occurrence of a specified value from a list. It takes the value to be removed as an argument and removes the first matching element from the list. If the specified value is not found in the list, it raises a ValueError.
print(a)  # Output: [1, 2, 4, 5]